      "classification": "valid_R3_structure",
      "reason": "The theorem is for every 1≤k≤N, not merely k≤p. The alternant quotient is integral. Its all-one evaluation is the binomial determinant/difference-product ratio. Each p-adic layer of the numerator has minimal pair count exactly at balanced occupancy, so the ratio is a p-unit iff all layers balance. Cyclotomic divisibility then precludes a singular node determinant. Orientation, denominator and k=1 conventions are correct."
    },
